{
  "_doc": "MASI v1.0 (Zeng et al., NAR 49:D776, 2021), all four downloads: the microbe-substance interaction records, the microbe-disease association records, the microbe dictionary and the substance dictionary. MASI is an AGGREGATOR of the primary literature, and this fragment is shaped by that one fact: 66.4% of its 12,512 interaction rows cite Maier 2018 or Zimmermann 2019, and 85.1% of the (taxon, compound) pairs it resolves to already carry an edge from one of those two screens. So its substances are their own node type rather than Drug nodes, its four interaction relationships are its own rather than METABOLISES / INHIBITS_GROWTH_OF, and the identity between a MASI substance and a graph Drug is a declared SAME_COMPOUND_AS edge -- one hop, never a merge. A query that wants what was MEASURED therefore never sees a re-curation of it, and a query that wants MASI's curated literature asks for it. Its 784 disease records are rows in core.json's shared taxon_condition.csv (a fourth source for ASSOCIATED_WITH) and fill 8 of the contract's 14 properties, the other six describing a study design this export has no column for. Its probiotic columns land on Taxon, written by prep_taxonomy.py, which is why that prep names masi in its DEPENDS_ON.",
  "_files": "Every table this fragment reads, declared once. A frame the build hands over by name; the preps fill it, nothing on disk backs it.",
